summary:
  Deezer's picture of the artist comes back as the track's cover.

history:
  For "Star Sisters - Waterloo" no catalogue had the song, and Deezer's
  picture of the artist is the sleeve of an album without it. It stood on
  the panel like the song's cover (seen 2026-11-12). The reader names it a
  picture of the artist. This mutant names it the track.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SearchLogic.js

find:
      var face = artDeezerReal(first.picture_big) || artDeezerReal(first.picture_medium);
      return face ? { "url": face, "kind": "artist" } : null;

replace:
      var face = artDeezerReal(first.picture_big) || artDeezerReal(first.picture_medium);
      return face ? { "url": face, "kind": "track" } : null;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_artkind.qml::test_deezers_artist_answer_is_a_picture_of_the_artist.
  Line-neutral.
